      "writtenOn": "2024-03-14T16:48:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "yes, there was no particularly good reason to remove *everything*, that was just a simple rule initially: if you open CCD and get acces to AP console you lose all TPM secrets so can\u0027t decrypt user or system data anymore if you did it on an owned device. and the simplest way you lose all TPM secrets is to remove all TPM objects. but we can be more selective.",
      "parentUuid": "cc0d4e5f_7c5ecaef",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 82,
